<table border="0" cellpadding="5" width="550" cellspacing="5" height="400" >
<tr valign="top" height="400" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<font face="arial" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Dear&nbsp;{!Contact.FirstName},</span></font><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><div><font face="arial">Thank you for your interest in undergraduate studies at the Herberger Institute for Design and the Arts School of Music at ASU. As one of the largest universities in the country, the ASU School of Music awards over $2 million to students annually, providing an excellent education at an unbeatable value. ASU's diverse and innovative community is a perfect complement to the personal attention you will receive in the School of Music. With a population of around 750 students, we offer small class sizes, state-of-the-art facilities and one-on-one instruction from world-renowned faculty. We invite you to consider the ASU School of Music for this important step in your music studies.</font></div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div>If you are interested in applying for fall 2017 admission, please first contact the School of Music Admissions office at&nbsp;<a href="mailto:musicadmissions@asu.edu">musicadmissions@asu.edu</a>&nbsp;to confirm that your desired program is accepting late applications. If you are interested in future study at ASU, please refer to the information below as a guideline for what to expect when you are ready to apply. For an idea of the course requirements for the various degree programs offered, select one of the checksheets accessible by your degree program of interest <a href="https://webapp4.asu.edu/programs/t5/programs/Keyword/music/undergrad/false">here</a>.&nbsp;</div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial">Eligibility, application, and admission information for transfer students can be found <a href="https://transfer.asu.edu/apply">here</a>. Please note that you are still required to complete a separate School of Music application and an audition to be considered for <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/undergraduate-steps-to-apply#Apply-to-the-School-of-Music">admission</a>. In addition, please utilize our <a href="https://webapp4.asu.edu/transfercreditguide/app/home">transfer credit guide</a> to see how your credits could <a href="https://transfer.asu.edu/transfer-credits">transfer to ASU</a>.</font></div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial"><a href="http://students.asu.edu/costs">Tuition and fees</a> at Arizona State University are reasonable, even for non-resident students. Financial aid, including academic scholarships, is available for both Freshman and Transfer applicants. Freshman applicants can use the Freshman Merit Scholarship Estimator to determine the amount they may be eligible to receive. Transfer applicants may learn about the New American University Transfer Scholarship <a href="http://students.asu.edu/node/7646">here</a>. In addition, music scholarship assistance is also available and awarded based on audition.</font></div></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b>Application Process</b></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b><br></b></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b>Step 1: Apply to ASU</b></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b>Step 2: Submit the School of Music Application</b></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b><br></b></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">You do not need to be admitted to the university prior to submitting your music application (Step 2).</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The School of Music requires a separate application from the university. Please visit the <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/undergraduate-steps-to-apply">School of Music website</a> for more details.&nbsp;</span></li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b>Step 3: Audition and Interview</b></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b><br></b></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">All applicants must perform an audition to be considered for admission to the School of Music.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">On-Campus auditions will not be scheduled until both applications are submitted.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Recorded auditions are acceptable when uploaded online. However, music scholarship consideration is prioritized to those who audition live.</span></li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Due to the high volume of applicants we receive each year, we recommend that you plan to apply as early as possible.&nbsp;</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br></span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-deadlines-fees">Application Deadline&nbsp;</a></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><b>Spring Admission: October 15 for all applicants except those applying to Music Composition.</b></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;">BM Composition applicants: Applications and prescreening portfolio must be received by <b>October 1</b>. Please visit <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/undergraduate-recordings-portfolios">our site</a> for more information.&nbsp;</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b>Fall Admission: January 4 for all applicants except those applying to Music Composition</b></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b><br></b></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">BM Composition: Prescreening portfolio must be received by <b>December 1</b>. Please visit <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/undergraduate-recordings-portfolios">our site</a> for more information.&nbsp;</font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><b>Audition Dates and Information</b></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><b><br></b></div><div><div><font face="arial">For complete audition dates and audition information please visit the <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/undergraduate-auditions">audition website</a>.&nbsp;</font></div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial">Recorded auditions (in lieu of live auditions) must be uploaded <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/undergraduate-recordings-portfolios">online</a> by <b>November 1</b> for spring admissions and <b>February 1</b> for fall admission. CD/DVD audition recordings are not accepted. To be considered for a music scholarship or teaching assistantship, a live, on-campus audition is preferred.</font></div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial">Ad hoc auditions may be scheduled with faculty (required for organ applicants, not available to voice applicants), but must be completed by <b>November 30</b> for spring admission and <b>February 28</b> for fall admission.</font></div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial">We welcome you to contact us via email at&nbsp;<a href="mailto:MusicAdmissions@asu.edu">MusicAdmissions@asu.edu</a> if you have any additional questions. We also encourage you to refer to the School of Music Web site, <a href="https://music.asu.edu/">music.asu.edu</a>, as a resource for your admissions questions.</font></div></div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial">Sincerely,</font></div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial">Office of Admissions</font></div><div><font face="arial">School of Music</font></div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial">Herberger Institute for Design and the Arts</font></div><div><font face="arial">Arizona State University</font></div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial"><a href="https://music.asu.edu/">music.asu.edu</a> | <a href="mailto:musicadmissions@asu.edu">musicadmissions@asu.edu</a></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><br></div>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>